+```text
+Aegis Event & ETL Specification for Causal Analysis
+
+Immutable event log (recommended fields):
+ - event_id: uuid
+ - timestamp: ISO8601 / epoch
+ - user_id / device_id
+ - experiment_id (nullable)
+ - assignment (treatment flag or bucket)
+ - action: string (e.g., "impression", "click", "purchase")
+ - treatment: binary or numeric (what was assigned)
+ - outcome(s): numeric or categorical fields (e.g., revenue, conversion)
+ - covariates: dictionary or exploded columns (demographics, pre-treatment metrics)
+ - randomization_seed: int (if applicable)
+ - provenance: {source, pipeline_version, ingestion_ts}
+
+Storage:
+ - Landing: object store (S3/GCS) as Parquet/JSON per day
+ - Processed: Delta/Parquet tables in data lake (Delta/Iceberg)
+
+ETL goals:
+ - Produce a "causal_ready" table with one row per unit with: id, treatment, outcome, covariates_snapshot, experiment_id, assignment_bucket, timestamp
+ - Ensure reproducibility: save ETL script/config and register dataset in MLflow with artifact pointing to dataset file(s)
+
+Security & Retention:
+ - Keep landing logs immutable
+ - Enforce access control; keep PII encrypted & only expose derived covariates for causal runs
+
